### Source delta: addon pairing token (GPL-3 §5a notice)

The addon source in `vendor/source/extension/**` is **unmodified upstream**. The
shipped zip is built from a staged copy with one documented delta, applied at
build time by `scripts/build-addon.mjs` from `patches/addon-pairing-token.mjs`:

| Modified file (inside the zip) | Change | Date |
|---|---|---|
| `transport.py` | `WebSocketClient(extra_headers=…)`; sends caller headers on the upgrade; rejects CR/LF in header names/values | 2026-11-27 |
| `config.py` | `GATEWAY_TOKEN_HEADER`, `GATEWAY_TOKEN_ENV`, `get_gateway_token()` (env `DSHBB_GATEWAY_TOKEN` → preference `gateway_token` → empty) | 2026-11-27 |
| `server.py` | dials with `x-dsh-bridge-token` on every (re)connect | 2026-11-27 |
| `ui/preferences.py` | `gateway_token` preference (PASSWORD subtype) + "Pairing Code" field in the connection box | 2026-11-27 |

Each modified file starts with a `# Modified by PI Blender Bridge 3.1.2 (2026-11-27)`
line, as GPL-3 §5a asks. The exact per-file before/after hashes are in
`vendor/PATCHES.lock.json`; the human-readable unified diff is
`patches/addon-pairing-token.diff`. `vendor/UPSTREAM.lock.json` still records the
unmodified upstream tree and is not rewritten by this delta.

